<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Hardened-runtime entitlements for SpektraFilm.

  This is intentionally empty.

  Notarization requires the hardened runtime, but the hardened runtime only
  demands entitlements for capabilities that gate code execution or sandbox
  access. SpektraFilm uses none of them:

    - no dlopen/dlsym, and no loading of unsigned plugins. The NSBundle calls in
      Native/src/SpektraMetalRenderer.mm look up bundled resources (the
      .metallib) by name; they never load executable code.
    - no JIT and no unsigned executable memory, so no
      com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit.
    - not sandboxed and not distributed through the Mac App Store, so no
      app-sandbox entitlement.
    - writes only to ~/Library/Application Support and ~/Library/Caches.
    - no XPC services and no bundled helper executables: the app ships a single
      binary, so there is no nested code left unsigned.
    - spawns /usr/bin/ssh (a system binary) from ProofDockService; that needs no
      entitlement under the hardened runtime.

  Do not add entitlements here speculatively. An entitlement the app does not
  need is a needless privilege, and Apple may reject a notarization request that
  asks for capabilities it cannot justify.

  If a future change adds plugin loading, JIT, or a helper binary, add the
  matching entitlement here and re-verify notarization.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict/>
</plist>